'''Season thirty-five''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' premiered on [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] and [[Disney+]] on September 15, 2026,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pedersen |first=Erik |date=July 27, 2026 |title=ABC Sets Fall Premiere Dates For Drama, Comedy & Reality Shows Including ''Grey’s Anatomy,'' ''Scrubs,'' ''DWTS,'' ''9-1-1'' Duo & More |url=https://deadline.com/2026/07/abc-fall-2026-premiere-dates-1237004718/ |access-date=July 29, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260727210806/https://deadline.com/2026/07/abc-fall-2026-premiere-dates-1237004718/|archive-date=July 27, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> and is scheduled to conclude on November 24, 2026.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/listings/2026/11/24/|title=Listings – November 24, 2026|publisher=[[The Futon Critic]]|quote=dancing with the stars: finale (#3512) [35th season finale]|access-date=September 18, 2026}}</ref> This season was the fourth to air live on both networks simultaneously. [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 19|Season nineteen]] champion [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] returned to host the installment, while former professional dancer and judge [[Julianne Hough]] returned as co-host.<ref name="TodayApril2026">{{Cite web |last=Calvario |first=Liz |date=April 22, 2026 |title=Maura Higgins and Ciara Miller to Compete on ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 |url=https://www.today.com/popculture/tv/maura-higgins-ciara-miller-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-rcna341538 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260423015343/https://www.today.com/popculture/tv/maura-higgins-ciara-miller-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-rcna341538 |archive-date=April 23, 2026 |access-date=April 23, 2026 |website=[[Today (American TV program)|Today]] |language=en}}</ref>

== Cast ==
=== Couples ===
On April 22, 2026, during an [[Upfront (advertising)|upfront]] for [[Hulu]]'s unscripted programming, [[Ciara Miller]] and [[Maura Higgins]] were announced as the first celebrity participants for the thirty-fifth season.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Strause |first=Jackie |date=April 22, 2026 |title=''Summer House'' Star Ciara Miller Cast in ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/summer-house-ciara-miller-dwts-1236571929/ |access-date=April 22, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260423003034/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/summer-house-ciara-miller-dwts-1236571929/|archive-date=April 23, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Jackson Olson]] joined the cast three weeks later during an upfront for [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]]'s original programming.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Shanfeld |first=Ethan |date=May 12, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Adds Savannah Bananas Player; Disney+ to Stream Live Banana Bowl Game |url=https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-savannah-bananas-1236746141/ |access-date=May 12, 2026 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260512214053/https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-savannah-bananas-1236746141/|archive-date=May 12, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> On June 17, [[TMZ]] reported that [[Guillermo Rodriguez (comedian)|Guillermo Rodriguez]] joined the cast;<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=June 17, 2026 |title=Jimmy Kimmel Sidekick Guillermo Rodriguez Joins ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 |url=https://www.tmz.com/2026/06/17/guillermo-rodriguez-joins-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35/ |access-date=June 18, 2026 |language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260618030750/https://www.tmz.com/2026/06/17/guillermo-rodriguez-joins-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35/|archive-date=June 18, 2026|url-status=live|publisher=[[TMZ]]}}</ref> [[Jimmy Kimmel]] confirmed Rodriguez's appearance later that day.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Shanfeld |first=Ethan |date=June 17, 2026 |title=Guillermo Rodriguez of ''Jimmy Kimmel Live!'' Joins ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 |url=https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/guillermo-jimmy-kimmel-dwts-season-35-1236784635/ |access-date=June 18, 2026 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260618033220/https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/guillermo-jimmy-kimmel-dwts-season-35-1236784635/|archive-date=June 18, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Throughout August, [[Tyler Cameron]], [[Jenna Dewan]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hudgins |first=Ryan |last2=Williams |first2=Amanda |date=August 19, 2026 |title=Tyler Cameron and Jenna Dewan Are Competing on ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35: Sources (Exclusive) |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/tyler-cameron-and-jenna-dewan-competing-on-dwts-season-35/ |access-date=August 19, 2026 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260820000022/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/tyler-cameron-and-jenna-dewan-competing-on-dwts-season-35/|archive-date=August 20, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Julia Stiles]], [[Tatyana Ali]],<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=August 20, 2026 |title=Julia Stiles and Tatyana Ali Competing on ''Dancing With The Stars'' |url=https://www.tmz.com/2026/08/20/julia-stiles-tatyana-ali-join-dwts/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260820234622/https://www.tmz.com/2026/08/20/julia-stiles-tatyana-ali-join-dwts/ |archive-date=August 20, 2026 |access-date=August 20, 2026 |publisher=[[TMZ]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Love Thy Nader|Sarah Jane Nader]] and [[The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives|Conner Leavitt]] were named to the cast.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Frank |first=Jason P. |date=August 21, 2026 |title=Julia Stiles Saved the Last Dance for ABC |url=https://www.vulture.com/article/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-cast.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260821211640/https://www.vulture.com/article/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-cast.html |archive-date=August 21, 2026 |access-date=August 21, 2026 |website=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]] |language=en}}</ref> Nader is the younger sister of [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 33|season thirty-three]] contestant [[Brooks Nader]], and Leavitt is the husband of [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 34|season thirty-four]] semi-finalist [[Whitney Leavitt]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harp |first=Justin |last2=Williams |first2=Amanda |date=August 20, 2026 |title=''DWTS'' Season 35 to Feature Whitney Leavitt’s Husband Conner, Brooks Nader’s Sister Sarah Jane |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dwts-casts-whitney-leavitts-husband-brooks-naders-sister/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260821000524/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dwts-casts-whitney-leavitts-husband-brooks-naders-sister/ |archive-date=August 21, 2026 |access-date=August 20, 2026 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US}}</ref> [[Amber Glenn]] and [[Ezra Frech]] became the first [[Winter Olympic Games|Olympic]] and [[Paralympic Games|Paralympic]] champions to compete during the same season.<ref>{{Cite news |date=September 3, 2026 |title=Olympic and Paralympic champions Amber Glenn and Ezra Frech to appear on ''Dancing with the Stars'' |url=https://www.olympics.com/en/news/amber-glenn-ezra-frech-dancing-with-the-stars |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260909173102/https://www.olympics.com/en/news/amber-glenn-ezra-frech-dancing-with-the-stars |archive-date=September 9, 2026 |access-date=September 9, 2026 |work=Olympics.com |publisher=[[International Olympic Committee]]}}</ref> 

The first celebrity-professional dancer pairing, Rodriguez and the reigning champion [[Witney Carson]], was announced on ''[[Good Morning America]]'' on August 17, 2026.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Blanchet |first=Brenton |date=August 17, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars''{{’}} Witney Carson Reveals Her Celebrity Partner for Season 35 |url=https://people.com/dancing-with-the-stars-witney-carson-reveals-her-celebrity-partner-season-35-12058401 |access-date=August 17, 2026 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/PcCEO|archive-date=August 17, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> At the time of the announcement, Carson was four months pregnant with her third child.<ref name="WCPregnant">{{Cite news |last=Sacks |first=Hannah |last2=Grant |first2=Kayla |last3=Tauber |first3=Michelle |date=August 17, 2026 |title=''DWTS'' Pro Witney Carson Is Pregnant, Expecting Baby No. 3 with Husband Carson McAllister (Exclusive) |url=https://people.com/dwts-pro-witney-carson-expecting-baby-no-3-with-husband-carson-mcallister-11872619 |access-date=August 17, 2026 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/hg4FB|archive-date=August 17, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> She became the first pro to enter an installment of ''Dancing with the Stars'' while pregnant,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Franklin |first=McKinley |date=August 17, 2026 |title=Witney Carson Is Pregnant and Returning for ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/witney-carson-pregnant-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-1236674102/ |access-date=August 17, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260817180102/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/witney-carson-pregnant-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-1236674102/|archive-date=August 17, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> and the first to compete that far into her second trimester.<ref name="WCPregnant" /> [[Gleb Savchenko]] and [[Sasha Farber]] did not return as pros this season,<ref>{{Cite web |date=September 2, 2026 |title=Why Isn't Gleb Savchenko in the ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Cast? |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/celebs/a73591798/why-isnt-gleb-on-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35/ |access-date=September 2, 2026 |website=[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]] |language=en-US|last=Bonner|first=Mehera|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260902171250/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/celebs/a73591798/why-isnt-gleb-on-dancing-with-the-stars-season-35/|archive-date=September 2, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> although Farber was still involved in other capacities.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dow |first=Marissa |date=September 16, 2026 |title=How Sasha Farber Returned to ''Dancing With the Stars'' for Season 35 Premiere Without Being a Pro |url=https://www.eonline.com/news/1436128/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-sasha-farbers-role-explained |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260916175829/https://www.eonline.com/news/1436128/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-sasha-farbers-role-explained |archive-date=September 16, 2026 |access-date=September 21, 2026 |website=[[E! News]]}}</ref> After a five-year hiatus, [[Sharna Burgess]] returned to the lineup on August 24.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Coleman |first=Ryan |date=August 24, 2026 |title=Sharna Burgess returning to ''Dancing With the Stars'' as a pro five years after surprise departure |url=https://ew.com/sharna-burgess-returning-to-dwts-as-pro-five-years-after-surprise-exit-12066061 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260824132715/https://ew.com/sharna-burgess-returning-to-dwts-as-pro-five-years-after-surprise-exit-12066061 |archive-date=August 24, 2026 |access-date=August 24, 2026 |work=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> [[Adele Zaikman]], winner of ''[[Dancing with the Stars: The Next Pro]]'', joined the series as a first-time pro on August 31.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Coleman |first=Ryan |date=August 31, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars: The Next Pro'' crowns [SPOILER] as first winner in dazzling finale |url=https://ew.com/dwts-the-next-pro-crowns-its-first-winner-in-thrilling-finale-12074744 |access-date=August 31, 2026 |work=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260901031946/https://ew.com/dwts-the-next-pro-crowns-its-first-winner-in-thrilling-finale-12074744|archive-date=September 1, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> She is the first [[Israelis|Israeli]] professional dancer to be featured on the series.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Karpen |first=Elizabeth |date=September 1, 2026 |title=Meet Adele Zaikman, the first Israeli pro on ''Dancing With the Stars'' |url=https://unpacked.media/meet-adele-zaikman-the-first-israeli-pro-on-dancing-with-the-stars/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260903200758/https://unpacked.media/meet-adele-zaikman-the-first-israeli-pro-on-dancing-with-the-stars/ |archive-date=September 3, 2026 |access-date=September 9, 2026 |website=[[Unpacked (website)|Unpacked]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Season thirty-four troupe member [[Hailey Bills]] was promoted to a first-time pro.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nesvig |first=Kara |date=September 2, 2026 |title=New ''Dancing with the Stars'' Pro Hailey Bills Says Getting the Job Is "Surreal" |url=https://www.teenvogue.com/story/20-year-old-hailey-bills-is-the-new-pro-on-dancing-with-the-stars |access-date=September 2, 2026 |website=[[Teen Vogue]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260902145100/https://www.teenvogue.com/story/20-year-old-hailey-bills-is-the-new-pro-on-dancing-with-the-stars|archive-date=September 2, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Her pairing with Nader marked the third same-sex partnership in the series' history, following [[JoJo Siwa]] & [[Jenna Johnson (dancer)|Jenna Johnson]] from [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 30|season thirty]] and [[Shangela]] & Savchenko from [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 31|season thirty-one]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Galante |first=Grace |date=August 20, 2026 |title=''DWTS'' Season 35 Will Feature First Same-Sex Partnership in 4 Years |url=https://parade.com/news/dwts-season-35-feature-same-sex-partnership-sarah-jane-nader-first-time-4-years |access-date=August 20, 2026 |work=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260821021325/https://parade.com/news/dwts-season-35-feature-same-sex-partnership-sarah-jane-nader-first-time-4-years|archive-date=August 21, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> 

The full roster of celebrity participants and their partnerships was revealed on ''Good Morning America'' on September 2.<ref name="GMA">{{Cite web |last=Bernabe |first=Angeline Jade |date=September 2, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' season 35: Meet the celebrity cast and their pro dance partners |url=https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-celebrity-cast/story?id=136095657 |access-date=September 2, 2026 |website=[[Good Morning America]] |publisher=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]] |language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260903214304/https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-celebrity-cast/story?id=136095657|archive-date=September 3, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> With sixteen couples, this season is tied with [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 9|season nine]] and season thirty-one as having the largest cast in the show's history.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Esquibias |first=Liza |last2=Goldstein |first2=Joelle |date=September 2, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' 2026 cast revealed – See who's competing in Season 35 |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2026/09/02/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-cast/91491311007/ |access-date=September 2, 2026 |website=[[USA Today]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260902151109/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2026/09/02/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-cast/91491311007/|archive-date=September 2, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

