=== Hosts and judges ===
The hosts and judges for the season were announced on ''Good Morning America'' on September 1, 2026, one day before the cast reveal.<ref>{{Cite press release |title=Programming Highlights for ABC News' ''Good Morning America'' and ''GMA3,'' Aug. 31 – Sept. 5 |date=August 28, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abcnews/pressrelease/programming-highlights-for-abc-news-good-morning-america-and-gma3-aug-31-sept-5/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=August 29, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260829135941/https://www.detpress.com/abcnews/pressrelease/programming-highlights-for-abc-news-good-morning-america-and-gma3-aug-31-sept-5/ |archive-date=August 29, 2026}}</ref> [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] and [[Julianne Hough]] returned as hosts,<ref name="S35HostsJudges">{{Cite web |last=Nardino |first=Meredith |date=September 1, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Judges and Hosts Revealed Before Premiere: Who’s Returning? |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-judges-and-hosts-revealed/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/SGT7w |archive-date=September 1, 2026 |access-date=September 1, 2026 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US}}</ref> while [[Derek Hough]], [[Carrie Ann Inaba]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] returned as judges.<ref name="S35HostsJudges" /> 

The second season of the ''Dancing with the Stars'' podcast, hosted by season thirty-four quarter-finalist [[Andy Richter]], launched on September 10.<ref name="S35PodcastParty">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' is Back in the Ballroom with an All-New Cast |date=September 1, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-is-back-in-the-ballroom-with-an-all-new-celebrity-cast-1/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=September 2, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260902132619/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-is-back-in-the-ballroom-with-an-all-new-celebrity-cast-1/|archive-date=September 2, 2026}}</ref> He revealed the majority of the season's themes during the second episode,<ref name="S35Themes">{{Cite news |last=Cohn |first=Paulette |date=September 18, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Themes for Season 35 Revealed |url=https://parade.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-themes-revealed |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260918195908/https://parade.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-themes-revealed |archive-date=September 18, 2026 |access-date=September 18, 2026 |work=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]]}}</ref> and shared the songs and dance styles for each week.<ref name="S&D">Season 35 song and dance styles:
*{{Cite web |last=Grebenyuk |first=Yana |date=September 10, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Premiere Songs and Dances Revealed After Surprise 2-Night Twist |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-premiere-songs-revealed/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260910203233/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-premiere-songs-revealed/ |archive-date=September 10, 2026 |access-date=September 10, 2026 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US}}
*{{Cite web |last=Grebenyuk |first=Yana |date=September 18, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Viral Hits Night Songs and Dances Revealed Before Week 2 |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-viral-hits-songs-revealed/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260919033920/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-viral-hits-songs-revealed/ |archive-date=September 19, 2026 |access-date=September 18, 2026 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US}}
